{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he said: For a hand upon the throne of Yah.</b> The meaning: when the kingship of the Holy One, blessed be He, prevails over His throne, then He will wage war against Amalek — and 'a hand' is an expression of kingship. And from there did Rabbi Eliezer, of blessed memory, [derive]. I heard that 'כי יד' refers to Amalek, because it troubles him that here it is written 'כי מחה אמחה את זכר עמלק,' while in the section Ki Tetze it is written 'תמחה את זכר עמלק.' There is no difficulty: this one — when he stretches out his hand against Israel — 'you shall erase'; that one — when he stretches out his hand against the Holy Temple — 'I shall erase,' for it is written 'a war for HaShem' — in His very Self and in His glory — 'against Amalek.' And Jerusalem is called the throne of the Holy One, blessed be He, and His throne is not complete until the seed of Amalek is eradicated, as it is written: 'וה' לעולם ישב, כונן למשפט כסאו.' And therefore the dead do not employ the name Yah, as it is written: 'לא המתים יהללויה' — because they cannot wage war against Amalek once they have died. Therefore David said: 'אֹדְךָ יְהֹוָה כִּי אֵלֶּהָ, כְּרַעֲךָ רַעְיָה' — and therefore said David: 'לא אמות כי אחיה ואספר מעשה יה,' 'יסור יסרני יה ולמות לא נתנני.' And it is written: 'אבוא במות יהללויה.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "The text after 'וה\"ל לעולם ישב' appears garbled; the verse cited as 'אדך ה לכי אלה' does not correspond to any biblical verse and is translated hyper-literally. The final citation 'אבוא במות יהללויה' is likewise obscure and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:27.422486511Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}